# This repository is edited on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) and built in WSL.
# Without this, a branch switch silently rewrites shell scripts with CRLF and
# they stop being executable by bash:
#
#   tools/verify_ref_md.sh: line 10: set: -: invalid option
#   line 27: syntax error near unexpected token `$'do\r''
#
# That has already cost one debugging round, and it fails in a way that looks
# like a broken script rather than a line-ending problem. Anything meant to be
# executed on the Linux side is pinned to LF here.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.m4    text eol=lf
*.am    text eol=lf
*.ac    text eol=lf
*.mk    text eol=lf
configure.ac  text eol=lf
autogen.sh    text eol=lf
